Date: Fri, 26 Feb 1993 10:53:27 -0500 (EST)
From: root@rmsdell.ftl.fl.us (Yanek Martinson)
Subject: ECON: betting simulator

Here's a  simple  perl script betting simulator, which you  can use to
try out the various betting/investment games discussed  earlier.  Just
change the payoff function and the strategy function accordingly.

Unmodified, this  script  simulates the game described by  Hal Finney,
where  you  get  half your money back with  60% probability, or double
your  money  back  with  40%  probability.   The  commented  out  line
implements the earlier  discussed scenario where your  money  randomly
either halves or doubles.

The  current  strategy  function will keep  half  your  money  in  the
investment,  readjusting  depending on how  much  you  won/lost.   The
commented out strategy function will put all your money into your bet.

Let me know if you get any interesting results using this program.

---- cut here for betsim.pl ----
#!/usr/bin/perl
$amt=100;           # initial amount
srand(time|$$);

while(1){
  $bet=$amt/2;      # decide how much to bet (strategy function)
# $bet=$amt;        # alternative strategy
  $amt-=$bet;       # place the bet (don't change this)
  if(rand<.6) {$win=$bet/2;} else {$win=$bet*2;}  # payoff function
# if(rand<.5) {$win=$bet/2;} else {$win=$bet*2;}  # alternative payoff
  $amt+=$win;       # add winnings to amount
  print $amt, "\n";
}
